      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Start",
      "title": "Before the operation",
      "learn": [
        "The Plusquamperfekt is the event before another past event. Ich hatte zu lange geschlafen. Vor der Operation hatte der Patient schon gegessen. Then the later event: Dann kam der Arzt.",
        "The participle is the same as in the Perfekt, and so is the choice of haben or sein. The auxiliary stands in the Präteritum: hat becomes hatte, ist becomes war. schlafen, essen, messen and schreiben take hatte. kommen and bleiben take war.",
        "hatte or war is in position 2. The participle stays at the end. Vor der Operation is position 1, so hatte follows it. vor takes the dative: vor der Operation.",
        "A spoken progress note still uses the Perfekt for a finished action. A state is still hatte or war with no participle. A modal stays konnte. The conjunction bevor comes in a later chapter. This chapter uses the preposition vor."
      ],
      "minutes": 25,
      "vocab": [
        { "de": "Patient", "article": "der", "plural": "die Patienten", "en": "patient (male)", "emoji": "🤒", "glossaryKey": "patient" },
